{
  "id": "suppressor-effect",
  "term": "suppressor effect",
  "definition": "In cognition research, a suppressor effect is an apparent finding in which a variable seems to improve prediction, but the pattern may actually be caused by multicollinearity between predictors rather than a real predictive relationship. Small samples can make this kind of artifact harder to rule out.",
